; A full garbage collection and GC-IMMEDIATELY complete on the 40-bit band
; (microcode 2001), and the system still works after them: a sample of the
; other checks follows.  The garbage collector reads the page hash table's
; first words as fixnums (DEALLOCATE-PAGES, sys2/gc.lisp), and the microcode's
; selective deposits into them (PGF-AG, AGER2, AGER4, XCPGS) must keep their
; tag: PHT1-ALL-BUT-SWAP-STATUS-CODE and PHT1-ALL-BUT-AGE-AND-SWAP-STATUS-CODE
; reach <39> (sys/ucadr/uc-page-fault.lisp).
(progn (si:gc-immediately) t) => T
(progn (si:full-gc) t) => T
(+ 1.0 2.0) => 3.0
(%pointer 0.1) => 1036831949
(1+ most-positive-fixnum) => 2147483648
(gcd most-negative-fixnum 0) => 2147483648
(let ((a (make-array 4 :initial-contents '(a b c d)))) (aref a 3)) => D
(array-in-bounds-p (make-array 4) -1) => NIL
(let ((x (make-instance 'si:property-list-mixin))) (send x :putprop 'blue 'color) (get x 'color)) => BLUE
(let ((a (make-array 3 :type 'art-float))) (aset 2.5 a 1) (list (aref a 0) (aref a 1))) => (0.0 2.5)
(let ((l (list 1 2 3))) (si:gc-immediately) (equal l '(1 2 3))) => T
